{%- comment -%}
  Carousel controls — prev · dots · next, under the track.

  Styles: ../component-library/css/components.css (.car__foot, .car__dots)
  Behaviour: assets/siwa-modules.js (initCarousel)

  The site's ONE control convention for horizontal rails. Every carousel
  is paged the same way, so a customer learns it once. Rendered from
  'carousel' and from the sections that still hold their own track
  markup, so the bar exists in exactly one place.

  Must sit inside an element carrying [data-siwa-carousel], after the
  track. The driver finds it by [data-carousel-foot].

  Both arrows draw the same glyph; prev is mirrored in CSS, and the
  mirroring swaps again under RTL. The glyph is rendered WITHOUT
  btn__icon--dir on purpose: .car__btn--prev already owns the mirroring,
  and the --dir modifier would flip it a second time. They disable at the
  ends rather than wrapping — a silent no-op reads as broken.

  The dots are built by the driver, not here: one dot is one PAGE, and
  how many slides make a page depends on the viewport, which Liquid
  cannot know. The bar ships hidden and is revealed only when there is
  more than one page.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="car__foot" data-carousel-foot hidden>
  <button class="car__btn car__btn--prev" type="button" data-carousel-prev
          aria-label="{{ 'collections.general.previous' | t }}">
    {%- render 'icon', name: 'arrow-right', class: 'btn__icon' -%}
  </button>
  <div class="car__dots" role="tablist" data-carousel-dots
       data-label="{{ 'collections.general.go_to_page' | t | escape }}"></div>
  <button class="car__btn car__btn--next" type="button" data-carousel-next
          aria-label="{{ 'collections.general.next' | t }}">
    {%- render 'icon', name: 'arrow-right', class: 'btn__icon' -%}
  </button>
</div>
